<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1559">1559</a>–<a href="/years/1632">1632</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly, was a Walloon general who commanded the army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholic-league">Catholic League</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. He won victories at the White Mountain in 1620, Wimpfen in 1622 and Lutter in 1626, and his army's sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magdeburg">Magdeburg</a> in 1631 became notorious. Defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustavus-adolphus">Gustavus Adolphus</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-breitenfeld-1631">Breitenfeld</a> in 1631, he was fatally wounded at the Lech in 1632.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/johann-tserclaes-count-of-tilly.jpg" alt="Johann Tserclaes, Count of Tilly" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Johann_Tserclaes_count_of_Tilly.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
